// BT-4930: PINS TODAY'S BEHAVIOUR; it does not endorse it. A cross-file
// `Foo >> sel => self delegate` on a `native:` class is a foreign extension
// fun, in which `self delegate` is a plain send. It does not call the backing
// module (`beamtalk_queue`, which has no `bt4930Probe/1`; if it did, the call
// would die with `undef`, not with the sentinel's error below). The send
// resolves to the `Object>>delegate` sentinel and raises a `user_error`.
//
// Queue is declared in stdlib/src/queue.bt, so this extension is cross-file.
// PIN-BUG(BT-4930): flip these assertions when the issue is decided.
//   option A: the definition is rejected or warned at compile time.
//   option B: the call reaches `beamtalk_queue:bt4930Probe/1` (undef).

Queue >> bt4930Probe -> Integer => self delegate

TestCase subclass: CrossFileSelfDelegateTest

  // Control: an inline `self delegate` on the same class reaches the backing module.
  testInlineDelegateReachesBackingModule =>
    self assert: Queue new size equals: 0

  // PIN-BUG(BT-4930): `delegate` resolves to the Object sentinel, not the backing module.
  testCrossFileDelegateReachesTheObjectSentinel =>
    self should: [Queue new perform: #bt4930Probe] raise: #user_error
    self assert: ([
      Queue new perform: #bt4930Probe
    ] on: Exception do: [:e |
      e message
    ]) equals: "delegate called on a non-native Object"
